  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760065,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1942 (NES) - Synopsis\n\nExperience the thrill of aerial combat in *1942* for the Nintendo Entertainment System, Capcom's breakout hit that took the arcade world by storm! Set in the Pacific Theater of World War II, this vertically scrolling shooter puts you in the cockpit of an American P-38 fighter plane, tasked with reaching Tokyo and dismantling the Japanese air fleet. Loosely based on the pivotal Battle of Midway, the game blends historical context with exhilarating gameplay.\n\nNavigate through waves of enemy aircraft and challenging obstacles, collecting power-ups to enhance your firepower and resilience. A unique \"roll\" feature allows you to evade enemy fire, adding a layer of strategic depth to the action. Featuring single-player and multiplayer modes, *1942* delivers intense, fast-paced action perfect for both seasoned gamers and newcomers alike. This classic title, selling over a million copies worldwide, remains a fondly remembered cornerstone of the NES library and a testament to Capcom's early success. Relive the golden age of arcade shooters!"
    },
